<article class="env-example" id="03U2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03U2">Example <span data-tag="03U2">64.14.5</span>.</a> Let $C = E$ be an elliptic curve and $\varphi = [n]$ be multiplication by $n$. Then $\varphi ^* = \varphi ^ t$ is multiplication by $n$ on the jacobian, so it has trace $2n$ and degree $n^2$. On the other hand, the fixed points of $\varphi $ are the points $p \in E$ such that $n p = p$, which is the $(n-1)$-torsion, which has cardinality $(n-1)^2$. So the theorem reads </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (n-1)^2 = 1 - 2n + n^2.  \]
</div>
